# Wild Idea Zone project family

Each project is its own repo hosted at `<subdomain>.wildideazone.com`. The main site, www.wildideazone.com (repo `~/code/wild-idea-zone`), is the hub. Every project ties back into it, and the hub lists every project.

## In the project (any stack)

1. **Logo:** copy `~/code/wild-idea-zone/public/favicon.svg` into the project as `wild-idea-zone.svg` (e.g. `src/assets/` or `public/`). Use the local copy instead of hotlinking.
2. **Favicon:** `<link rel="icon" href="…/wild-idea-zone.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />`, unless the project has its own icon.
3. **Header logo link:** put the logo (24–32px) just left of the project title, linking to the hub:
   ```html
   <a class="wiz-home" href="https://www.wildideazone.com/" title="Wild Idea Zone: more projects">
     <img src="./src/assets/wild-idea-zone.svg" alt="Wild Idea Zone" width="28" height="28" />
   </a>
   ```
4. **Footer credit:** a small, muted line at the bottom of the main layout. `<slug>` is the project's slug on the hub:
   ```html
   <footer class="wiz-footer">
     A <a href="https://www.wildideazone.com/">Wild Idea Zone</a> project ·
     <a href="https://www.wildideazone.com/projects/<slug>">About this build</a> ·
     <a href="https://www.wildideazone.com/projects">More projects</a>
   </footer>
   ```
5. **Meta:** add `<meta property="og:site_name" content="Wild Idea Zone" />`.
6. **README:** link the live subdomain and the hub page `https://www.wildideazone.com/projects/<slug>`.

Style the links with the project's own accent color and fonts; only the logo is shared. Keep them out of the way of the app itself. Full-screen games and canvases must still fit the viewport.

## On the hub (`~/code/wild-idea-zone`)

- Add an entry to `src/data/projects.ts`: `slug`, `title`, `tagline`, `description`, `highlights`, `tags`, `status`, `subdomain`, `repoUrl`, `image`, and `featured` when it should appear on the home page.
- Put the card image at `public/projects/<slug>/` as a 1024px-wide JPEG screenshot.
- Run `npm run lint && npm run build`, then `npm run deploy`. There is no CI.

## Hosting the subdomain

- Cloudflare DNS (zone `wildideazone.com`): `CNAME <subdomain> → dwisnowski.github.io`, **DNS only** (grey cloud), for GitHub Pages.
- GitHub Pages: set the source to GitHub Actions and the custom domain to `<subdomain>.wildideazone.com`, then turn on Enforce HTTPS once the certificate is approved.
